WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:01.680
- All right, so we
always like to close out

00:00:01.680 --> 00:00:03.000
with something trending online

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:03.990
that might make you smile.

00:00:03.990 --> 00:00:05.080
This is what I'm liking.

00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:07.497
(rock music)

00:00:08.430 --> 00:00:10.350
So I recently dropped a couple songs

00:00:10.350 --> 00:00:11.940
off my upcoming album "Chemistry"

00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:13.260
and I'm super excited about it,

00:00:13.260 --> 00:00:16.904
but this is my favorite thing
to happen since I released it.

00:00:16.904 --> 00:00:19.500
It also led to something
I did not see coming.

00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:22.290
Apparently Australian singer, Troye Sivan

00:00:22.290 --> 00:00:24.837
thought I was calling him
out in my song "Mine."

00:00:25.830 --> 00:00:29.250
I died, you guys, when I
saw this, I laughed so hard.

00:00:29.250 --> 00:00:30.660
Somebody sent it to me, I'd just woken up.

00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:34.110
I laughed so hard alone in
my house, belly laughed.

00:00:34.110 --> 00:00:35.943
Just look at what he posted on TikTok.

00:00:35.943 --> 00:00:40.110
- What did I do to upset Kelly Clarkson?

00:00:40.110 --> 00:00:43.228
♪ Troye Sivan ♪

00:00:43.228 --> 00:00:47.645
♪ Who the hell do you think you are? ♪

00:00:50.080 --> 00:00:51.025
(audience cheering)

00:00:51.025 --> 00:00:54.570
It's hands down my favorite thing

00:00:54.570 --> 00:00:57.600
that's ever happened
with releasing a song.

00:00:57.600 --> 00:01:01.173
I cannot not think of him
when I sing this song now.

00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:05.220
Every time I'm like
Troye Sivan, every time.

00:01:05.220 --> 00:01:08.580
To be clear, I did not sing his name.

00:01:08.580 --> 00:01:09.900
I don't know why it sounds like that,

00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:12.600
but the line is "your choice of art."

00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:14.190
And I guess it's just so high, right?

00:01:14.190 --> 00:01:16.230
It just, I don't know,
it's just I sound a little

00:01:16.230 --> 00:01:18.300
and who the hell do you
think you are is the line.

00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:21.120
But I have Troye on the
line to clear things up.

00:01:21.120 --> 00:01:22.740
He watches on 7 Bravo.

00:01:22.740 --> 00:01:23.905
What's up, man?

00:01:23.905 --> 00:01:26.820
(audience cheering)

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:29.190
You are, first of all,
I've already been a fan,

00:01:29.190 --> 00:01:31.773
but man, you are the funniest human.

00:01:32.910 --> 00:01:34.110
Sorry for the mix up.

00:01:34.110 --> 00:01:35.340
How did you find that out?

00:01:35.340 --> 00:01:37.020
How did you hear that?

00:01:37.020 --> 00:01:37.890
- Well, first of all,

00:01:37.890 --> 00:01:40.530
I'm sorry to be meeting
this way with like a fight.

00:01:40.530 --> 00:01:41.363
You know what I mean?

00:01:41.363 --> 00:01:43.620
'Cause I love you so much
and I have for so long.

00:01:43.620 --> 00:01:45.630
But no, my friend texted it to me

00:01:45.630 --> 00:01:47.460
and literally was like, "What did you do?

00:01:47.460 --> 00:01:49.620
How did you upset Kelly Clarkson?"

00:01:49.620 --> 00:01:50.490
And I watched it

00:01:50.490 --> 00:01:52.770
and just immediately I
had the same reaction.

00:01:52.770 --> 00:01:55.080
I was like belly laughing
'cause it's so scary.

00:01:55.080 --> 00:01:57.450
You're so sincere when you sing it as well

00:01:57.450 --> 00:02:00.210
that I was like, "Oh
my God, what did I do?"

00:02:00.210 --> 00:02:02.539
But, and then I immediately
like opened TikTok

00:02:02.539 --> 00:02:03.690
and made the TikTok.

00:02:03.690 --> 00:02:06.240
- Oh my god, it was hilarious.

00:02:06.240 --> 00:02:07.410
And thank you so much.

00:02:07.410 --> 00:02:09.630
I laughed so hard I worked out.

00:02:09.630 --> 00:02:11.790
Anyway, I hear you that
you have a lot of projects

00:02:11.790 --> 00:02:13.590
going on these days, so
tell me what you're up to.

00:02:13.590 --> 00:02:14.730
- I do, yeah.

00:02:14.730 --> 00:02:16.830
My album is pretty much done.

00:02:16.830 --> 00:02:17.663
So that's coming out soon.

00:02:17.663 --> 00:02:19.026
- Yeah!

00:02:19.026 --> 00:02:21.060
- I'm also on a TV show on HBO

00:02:21.060 --> 00:02:23.880
that's called "The Idol"
that's coming out in June.

00:02:23.880 --> 00:02:25.320
So very excited.

00:02:25.320 --> 00:02:26.153
- [Kelly] That's incredible.

00:02:26.153 --> 00:02:27.323
- I'm gonna make this my
theme song by the way.

00:02:27.323 --> 00:02:30.095
Anytime I do any promo or
anything for any of that,

00:02:30.095 --> 00:02:31.560
it's gonna play your song.

00:02:31.560 --> 00:02:33.030
I'm gonna make people do that.

00:02:33.030 --> 00:02:35.040
- Oh my god, I love it so much.

00:02:35.040 --> 00:02:35.978
I literally, man,

00:02:35.978 --> 00:02:38.430
I played a show the other
night playing my whole record

00:02:38.430 --> 00:02:40.170
and like right when it comes, like,

00:02:40.170 --> 00:02:41.670
I can't not think of you.

00:02:41.670 --> 00:02:43.710
And then I have to be like, don't laugh.

00:02:43.710 --> 00:02:46.076
It's not a funny part emotionally,

00:02:46.076 --> 00:02:48.420
but it's the funniest thing ever.

00:02:48.420 --> 00:02:50.010
Anyway, thank you so much, Troye.

00:02:50.010 --> 00:02:50.940
There probably so much joy.

00:02:50.940 --> 00:02:51.840
I promise, we're cool.

00:02:51.840 --> 00:02:52.770
We're not in a fight.

00:02:52.770 --> 00:02:54.330
I'm liking your post right now.

00:02:54.330 --> 00:02:56.011
I can't wait for your music, man.

00:02:56.011 --> 00:02:56.844
(audience cheering)

00:02:56.844 --> 00:02:58.264
- [Troye] Thank you so much.

00:02:58.264 --> 00:02:59.097
- Absolutely.

00:02:59.097 --> 00:03:01.140
Well, okay, so usually this is the point

00:03:01.140 --> 00:03:02.550
we give our guest $1,000

00:03:02.550 --> 00:03:04.860
courtesy of our season
long partner Pilot Pen,

00:03:04.860 --> 00:03:06.780
makers of FriXion, the go-to erasable pen

00:03:06.780 --> 00:03:07.680
of "The Kelly Clarkson Show."

00:03:07.680 --> 00:03:09.390
But as you just heard,

00:03:09.390 --> 00:03:10.890
Troye's doing pretty well for himself.

00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:12.450
He's all right, so he doesn't need it.

00:03:12.450 --> 00:03:15.142
So we're giving the money
to someone in the audience.

00:03:15.142 --> 00:03:17.043
(audience cheering)

00:03:17.043 --> 00:03:21.450
So, it's actually taped
beneath one of your chairs.

00:03:21.450 --> 00:03:23.310
So we don't know who has it right now.

00:03:23.310 --> 00:03:24.143
So who has it?

00:03:26.239 --> 00:03:27.119
- What?

00:03:27.119 --> 00:03:30.119
(audience cheering)

00:03:35.347 --> 00:03:36.264
- Stand up.

00:03:37.622 --> 00:03:38.979
- Oh my God.

00:03:38.979 --> 00:03:40.530
- First of all, you are adorable

00:03:40.530 --> 00:03:42.000
with your little fanny pack.

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:42.870
- Thank you.
- I like it.

00:03:42.870 --> 00:03:43.703
- Thank you so much.

00:03:43.703 --> 00:03:45.570
- It's so nineties, your vibe right now.

00:03:45.570 --> 00:03:46.440
What's your name?

00:03:46.440 --> 00:03:48.450
- My name is Charlene.
- So what are you gonna do?

00:03:48.450 --> 00:03:50.070
Don't just spend it on bills.

00:03:50.070 --> 00:03:52.890
Spend a little on bills,
then have fun with it.

00:03:52.890 --> 00:03:54.450
What would you spend it on?

00:03:54.450 --> 00:03:55.680
- I'm like school.

00:03:55.680 --> 00:03:58.530
I'm finishing my bachelor's right now.

00:03:58.530 --> 00:04:00.451
My goal is to get my master's in nursing.

00:04:00.451 --> 00:04:01.527
- [Kelly] That's incredible.

00:04:01.527 --> 00:04:03.727
That's incredible.

00:04:03.727 --> 00:04:04.560
- I probably will spend it on school.

00:04:04.560 --> 00:04:08.250
- Actually, that's probably
a smart decision, Charlene.

00:04:08.250 --> 00:04:09.700
Thank you so much for coming.

